1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:24,640
Ms. Frieren.

4
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:28,770
You're late.

5
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,700
You defeated Aura, didn't you?

6
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:50,080
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

7
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,500
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,420
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

9
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:57,050
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

10
00:00:57,050 --> 00:00:59,380
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

11
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:01,720
<i>Across this land</i>

12
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:04,050
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

13
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:06,520
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

14
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:18,820
<i>The story ends</i>

15
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:21,320
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

16
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,160
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

17
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,830
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

18
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:28,330
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

19
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:30,500
<i>Makes people forget</i>

20
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,290
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

21
00:01:33,290 --> 00:01:35,090
<i>Begin to rust</i>

22
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:36,920
<i>Just the same</i>

23
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,220
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

24
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:42,550
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

25
00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:44,430
<i>And they live on</i>

26
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:46,970
<i>We chose the same path</i>

27
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:49,100
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

28
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,640
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

29
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:54,900
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

30
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,270
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

31
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:57,360
<i>Even now</i>

32
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,740
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

33
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:03,280
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

34
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,950
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

35
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:26,130
I don't believe—
I <i>can't</i> believe this happened.

36
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:27,090
Let's go.

37
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:30,210
Wait. You don't need to run.

38
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:33,600
The graf said he'd pardon you.

39
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:38,360
It must have been a fierce battle,

40
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:41,870
but none of them are seriously damaged.

41
00:02:44,930 --> 00:02:51,110
Thank you for treating the heroes
of the northern lands with respect.

42
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:59,340
I used to cast flashier spells,
but Himmel got mad at me.

43
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:01,370
I bet he did.

44
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:04,340
He was right to be angry. I'd be angry, too.

45
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:08,130
Mr. Himmel trained you well.

46
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:09,730
Don't say it like that.

47
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:13,300
I guess you're right, though.

48
00:03:16,330 --> 00:03:18,720
This is a normal reaction.

49
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:20,800
What do you mean?

50
00:03:21,790 --> 00:03:23,440
Don't worry about it.

51
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:27,070
Fern, Stark.

52
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:29,810
Good job defeating Lügner and his henchwoman.

53
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,580
I'm proud of you.

54
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,920
I'd be even more impressed
if you weren't so beat up, though.

55
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,080
This is normal for a warrior.

56
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:43,070
What does "normal" even mean?

57
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:44,720
You're covered in wounds.

58
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:49,520
See that they receive proper burials.
I'll escort our benefactors to the city.

59
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,360
Yes, milord.

60
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,640
Milord.

61
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:53,980
What is it?

62
00:04:05,630 --> 00:04:06,950
Frieren.

63
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:11,740
I've never been as grateful to anyone
as I am to you today.

64
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:32,120
Frieren, I promised to reward you
in any way I could.

65
00:04:33,410 --> 00:04:38,100
You requested the defensive
barrier grimoire by Flamme

66
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:43,140
that has been passed down
for generations in my family.

67
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:47,650
Are you sure this is what you want?
This grimoire...

68
00:04:47,650 --> 00:04:48,980
It's fake.

69
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:54,470
Yes. The defensive barrier it describes

70
00:04:54,470 --> 00:04:58,680
is nothing like our city's barrier,
whose spell is passed down by oral tradition.

71
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,590
I'm well aware of that, milord.

72
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:03,300
It's just my hobby.

73
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,170
I see.

74
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:10,000
Either way, you needn't use
such formal language.

75
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,550
From your perspective,
I must seem akin to an infant.

76
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:18,440
I suffered a bitter experience when
I first left to defeat the Demon King.

77
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:22,100
Come to think of it, Mr. Heiter
said that in the royal capital,

78
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:25,510
disrespecting nobility
is punishable by death.

79
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:31,070
Himmel and Eisen were nearly executed
for speaking casually to the king.

80
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:35,670
Remembering Himmel screaming
and crying takes me back.

81
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,570
Execution? That's extreme.

82
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:45,660
And speaking so casually to me
is a serious crime in this town, brat.

83
00:05:45,890 --> 00:05:47,290
Sorry, old man.

84
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:49,490
I'm gonna break this
expensive-looking chair.

85
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:54,600
Th-The central lands sure
are barbaric, milord.

86
00:05:58,410 --> 00:05:59,970
Seriously?

87
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:02,750
I've finished cutting the
trees in the backyard.

88
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:03,730
Thank you.

89
00:06:05,030 --> 00:06:09,980
Well, you know, I only said that
so you'd escape.

90
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:14,870
In this town, you won't be thrown
in prison just for speaking casually.

91
00:06:15,230 --> 00:06:17,180
Be at ease.

92
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:19,810
In that case...

93
00:06:19,810 --> 00:06:22,120
Good news for you, Mr. Stark.

94
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:26,870
He's passed out.

95
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:36,510
I've told the townsfolk of Aura's defeat.

96
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:39,990
They all want to honor the heroes.

97
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,570
I ask that you take your time here.

98
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:54,890
He's floating.

99
00:06:57,780 --> 00:07:00,290
It's not that big a deal.

100
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:13,330
<i>The name that has protected me</i>

101
00:07:13,330 --> 00:07:20,580
<i>Is being called by that soothing voice of yours</i>

102
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:27,770
<i>So that you won't close your eyes all alone</i>

103
00:07:27,770 --> 00:07:35,020
<i>I'll embrace you</i>

104
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:42,010
<i>You joined your warm hands with mine</i>

105
00:07:42,010 --> 00:07:48,070
<i>So I won't forget</i>

106
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:55,210
<i>Beyond the night, where it's full of flowers</i>

107
00:07:55,210 --> 00:08:02,430
<i>It is where you are, a place I will return to</i>

108
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:10,040
<i>Split the swelling, unravel the darkness</i>

109
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:18,020
<i>So that the dream remains uncorrupted</i>

110
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:23,460
<i>To the blue path that never ends</i>

111
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,080
I finished the shopping.

112
00:08:26,070 --> 00:08:28,150
Shall we go, then?

113
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:31,930
You're leaving already, Frieren?

114
00:08:31,930 --> 00:08:33,410
Graf Granat.

115
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,990
I'll see you to the gates.

116
00:08:41,170 --> 00:08:44,880
Frieren, I hear you're traveling to Ende,

117
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:48,090
the farthest point north,
where the Demon King's castle is.

118
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:54,360
But currently, conditions on the
Northern Plateau aren't looking good.

119
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:57,200
Travel is restricted.

120
00:08:57,610 --> 00:09:02,880
Even adventurers must be accompanied
by a first-class mage.

121
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:06,820
Then there should no problem
with Ms. Frieren by our side.

122
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:09,740
What's a first-class mage?

123
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:12,270
Ms. Frieren, you don't know?

124
00:09:12,870 --> 00:09:17,200
It's a certification awarded by the
Continental Magic Association.

125
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,280
Certification?

126
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:21,550
I acquired mine in the
holy capital when we left.

127
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,370
See?

128
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:26,230
This is my third-class mage certificate.

129
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:30,110
Come to think of it, you did have
some business to take care of then.

130
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:32,560
Is this what certifications
look like these days?

131
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:37,120
Ms. Frieren, don't tell me you're
an uncertified underground mage.

132
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:39,420
Don't make it sound like
I'm some back-alley doctor.

133
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:44,430
The organizations that regulate
mages are constantly changing.

134
00:09:44,430 --> 00:09:47,060
I can't be bothered obtaining
a new certification every time.

135
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:51,300
I doubt this holy emblem works anymore.

136
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:55,480
What is that antique?

137
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:59,020
Even I know about the
Continental Magic Association.

138
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,940
They've been around for over
half a century at the very least.

139
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:03,800
That's barely anything.

140
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:08,740
It's a hassle when they change their
standards of conduct so frequently.

141
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:12,030
In any case, we'll need to overcome
this problem before we continue.

142
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:15,820
I don't know the specifics,

143
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,950
but I believe there's a place
in the northern lands

144
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:20,670
where you can take the first-class exam.

145
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:26,510
The largest magical city in the
northern lands, Äußerst.

146
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,440
It's far beyond the Schwer Mountains.

147
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:35,240
You can follow the highway,
but it'll be a long journey.

148
00:10:38,870 --> 00:10:43,460
Frieren, the house of Granat will
never forget what you've done for us.

149
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,510
Safe travels.

150
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:02,340
It's snowing.

151
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:04,450
It's almost winter.

152
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:09,130
The winters around here are bitter,
so be careful.

153
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,350
If you underestimate them, you'll die.

154
00:11:11,350 --> 00:11:13,110
Is it really that dangerous?

155
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,620
Don't you know?

156
00:11:16,110 --> 00:11:20,130
In the war against the Demon King's forces,
what do you think claimed the most lives?

157
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:23,000
It was the winters of the northern lands.

158
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:32,630
See? We're lost.

159
00:11:37,470 --> 00:11:38,780
What are we going to do?

160
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:47,240
We're lost.

161
00:11:47,970 --> 00:11:53,010
I can't believe we got lost before
even entering the Schwer Mountains.

162
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:56,570
Mr. Stark, wake up!

163
00:11:56,570 --> 00:11:57,750
If you fall asleep, you'll die!

164
00:11:59,530 --> 00:12:04,030
Have jumbo-berry specials
always been this small?

165
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:05,380
Who cares about that right now?

166
00:12:06,530 --> 00:12:07,840
What should we do?

167
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:12,770
In these strong winds,
we can't transport him with magic.

168
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:15,410
He'd probably be blown away.

169
00:12:16,810 --> 00:12:19,160
Then we'll have to carry him.

170
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,010
He's heavy.

171
00:12:27,710 --> 00:12:30,400
Why is he so heavy?

172
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:33,170
You smell nice.

173
00:12:33,170 --> 00:12:34,920
Can I leave him behind?

174
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,030
Bear it for now.

175
00:12:36,450 --> 00:12:39,650
There should be an emergency shelter
at the foot of the mountains.

176
00:12:39,650 --> 00:12:42,660
Isn't that information
eighty years out of date?

177
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:44,880
Are we going to be all right?

178
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,300
Good.

179
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:57,080
It's still being maintained regularly.

180
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:04,370
It seems like someone's inside.

181
00:13:04,370 --> 00:13:06,510
Perhaps someone arrived before us.

182
00:13:06,510 --> 00:13:08,560
We're going inside.

183
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,650
We'll freeze out here.

184
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,650
Good! Very good!

185
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:19,040
I'm starting to feel warmer!

186
00:13:26,330 --> 00:13:27,670
Excuse the intrusion.

187
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,810
Ms. Frieren, we can't stay here.
Let's look for someplace else.

188
00:13:34,810 --> 00:13:36,590
What? Why?

189
00:13:36,590 --> 00:13:38,670
There's a pervert inside.

190
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,670
A pervert? That's awfully rude.

191
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:45,570
Let's go, Ms. Frieren.

192
00:13:46,650 --> 00:13:49,260
Wait. Are you an elf?

193
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:58,340
It's been about 300 years since
I've met another of my kind.

194
00:13:58,730 --> 00:14:01,980
I thought the elves had already died out.

195
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:03,500
So did I.

196
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:06,700
And thanks for the fire, miss.

197
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,330
Not at all.

198
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:11,640
I'm lucky I ran into a couple of mages.

199
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:14,940
The Goddess must have led you here.

200
00:14:15,670 --> 00:14:21,130
I crossed the Schwer Mountains,
but this blizzard extinguished my coals.

201
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:25,240
I was keeping myself alive by doing
squats inside this freezing hut.

202
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:26,780
I see.

203
00:14:27,230 --> 00:14:29,230
I'm not sure I understand.

204
00:14:30,010 --> 00:14:31,990
I'm Kraft the Monk.

205
00:14:32,250 --> 00:14:34,310
Frieren the Mage.

206
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:36,610
Fern, also a mage.

207
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,750
This is Mr. Stark the Warrior.

208
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,700
Anyway, Aureole, huh?

209
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:44,530
You're traveling to heaven, then?

210
00:14:45,410 --> 00:14:47,960
Good on you for being so pious.

211
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,430
I'm not sure I totally believe it.

212
00:14:50,950 --> 00:14:52,170
Ms. Frieren.

213
00:14:52,950 --> 00:14:54,840
Mr. Stark is getting colder.

214
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:03,680
<i>So warm and comfortable...</i>

215
00:15:04,970 --> 00:15:09,240
<i>And that's one huge jumbo-berry special.</i>

216
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:14,040
<i>What happened to me?</i>

217
00:15:15,330 --> 00:15:17,620
<i>We got caught in a blizzard, and then...</i>

218
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,640
Who is this guy?

219
00:15:38,770 --> 00:15:40,880
You're so noisy.

220
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:46,620
That's no way to thank someone
for warming you up with their body.

221
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:48,630
Their body?

222
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,510
You've got a nice body, old man.

223
00:15:53,510 --> 00:15:54,640
Mr. Stark?

224
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:56,660
No, not like that.

225
00:15:57,650 --> 00:16:00,380
I mean he's got a nice body
from training hard.

226
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:04,000
You must be really strong.

227
00:16:04,450 --> 00:16:06,040
What's your name?

228
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,590
Kraft the Monk.

229
00:16:09,290 --> 00:16:11,370
I've never heard of you.

230
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:15,180
But you must be a pretty famous monk, right?

231
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:20,000
Stark, rest here.

232
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:23,290
You two, help me bring in food supplies.

233
00:16:23,850 --> 00:16:26,680
My wagon and cargo are nearby.

234
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:32,020
I'm really glad I met all of you.

235
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:35,360
We'll be able to use these frozen supplies.

236
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:37,420
Use as much as you'd like.

237
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,110
You've certainly stocked up.

238
00:16:40,530 --> 00:16:44,160
Trying to cross the Schwer Mountains
in these conditions would be suicide.

239
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,240
We're stuck here for a while.

240
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:53,640
By the way, Frieren, do you know who I am?

241
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:54,930
Not at all.

242
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:55,960
I didn't think so.

243
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:59,190
I don't know the first thing
about you, either.

244
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:02,290
She's the mage from the party of heroes.

245
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:04,130
And before that?

246
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:07,030
What do you mean?

247
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:10,060
I mean that we're elves.

248
00:17:59,610 --> 00:18:01,560
It's been nearly six months.

249
00:18:02,370 --> 00:18:07,590
Thanks to all of you, we made it through
the long winter in the northern lands.

250
00:18:09,190 --> 00:18:10,240
Take this.

251
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:18,350
Give it to Fern. She's a pious girl.

252
00:18:18,950 --> 00:18:21,410
Must be because she was raised by a priest.

253
00:18:22,110 --> 00:18:24,640
She never forgets to thank the Goddess.

254
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:28,430
Kraft, why do you believe in the Goddess?

255
00:18:29,630 --> 00:18:32,810
You don't, do you?

256
00:18:33,430 --> 00:18:37,520
Excluding during the age of mythology,

257
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:43,130
the Goddess of Creation hasn't shown herself
once in the long history of this world.

258
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:47,900
You're young. I used to think that way, too.

259
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:52,570
But now I believe in the Goddess
from the bottom of my heart.

260
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:57,080
No, I need her to exist.

261
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:04,260
Everyone who knew of my
righteous triumphs has died.

262
00:19:05,510 --> 00:19:10,220
So when I die, I'll go to heaven
and the Goddess will praise me.

263
00:19:11,330 --> 00:19:13,850
She'll say, "Well done, Kraft."

264
00:19:14,450 --> 00:19:18,930
"You lived a fantastic life."

265
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:23,490
You understand that, Frieren.

266
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:30,820
It's too cruel for the path your life took
to not be remembered by anyone.

267
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:36,250
We've lived a long time to get to this point.

268
00:19:38,670 --> 00:19:42,820
Kraft, that's just something we desire.

269
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:45,140
You're right.

270
00:19:47,550 --> 00:19:50,130
Does that apply to heaven too, Frieren?

271
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:57,910
No matter.

272
00:19:58,470 --> 00:20:01,770
Tell me about yourself,
and I'll tell you about myself.

273
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:08,520
If you don't believe in the Goddess,
then I'll praise you instead.

274
00:20:12,430 --> 00:20:14,030
Are you surprised?

275
00:20:14,030 --> 00:20:20,050
Yeah. I didn't think you'd fund the
reconstruction of this village's orphanage.

276
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:23,870
You don't beat around the bush, do you?

277
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:27,030
I was an orphan, too.

278
00:20:30,750 --> 00:20:36,560
I'm sure the Goddess will praise me
for living a pure and proper life.

279
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:41,080
What are you talking about, you corrupt
priest? You're drinking right now.

280
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:43,090
Frieren.

281
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:47,560
Do you have someone to praise you?

282
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,070
Where did that come from?

283
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:54,290
You don't seem to believe in the Goddess,

284
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:59,500
so if you tell me about yourself,
I'll praise you instead.

285
00:21:00,390 --> 00:21:02,660
I haven't done much with my life.

286
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:05,840
I haven't done anything praiseworthy.

287
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,840
Even though you're constantly
suppressing your mana?

288
00:21:10,970 --> 00:21:15,530
To me, that seems like the
result of tremendous effort.

289
00:21:16,470 --> 00:21:19,230
Something that would take
a lifetime to accomplish.

290
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:22,300
You noticed?

291
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:25,600
How many years have we
traveled together again?

292
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:28,870
It's not an interesting story.

293
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,580
I don't mind.

294
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:33,520
Besides, it sounds like something
useful to know for the future.

295
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:34,250
Why?

296
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:39,630
Perhaps a child of mine will become a mage.

297
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:44,150
I thought priests couldn't marry.

298
00:21:50,260 --> 00:21:54,940
Why do so many strange
people serve the Goddess?

299
00:21:55,970 --> 00:22:00,400
I'll pass. I've already had
someone else praise me.

300
00:22:02,330 --> 00:22:06,520
I see. You have good friends, Frieren.

301
00:22:06,810 --> 00:22:07,970
You should cherish them.

302
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:12,050
Actually, he's already...

303
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:19,540
He's in heaven now.

304
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:22,600
Then you'll see him again someday.

305
00:22:23,590 --> 00:22:24,840
You're right.

306
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:29,060
I'm going this way.

307
00:22:29,650 --> 00:22:33,000
Frieren, I doubt this is
the last time we'll meet.

308
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:35,930
I'll see you in a few centuries.

309
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:42,930
Take care, old man! I had fun!

310
00:22:43,810 --> 00:22:47,250
Thank you for the pendant!

311
00:22:49,990 --> 00:22:52,530
<i>And you alright</i>

312
00:22:53,030 --> 00:22:55,040
<i>Can you hear me</i>

313
00:22:55,830 --> 00:23:01,920
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

314
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:04,250
<i>Crying excessively</i>

315
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:07,420
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

316
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:13,470
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

317
00:23:13,470 --> 00:23:17,180
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

318
00:23:17,180 --> 00:23:19,940
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

319
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:25,610
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

320
00:23:25,610 --> 00:23:29,150
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

321
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:32,200
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

322
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:36,950
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

323
00:23:36,950 --> 00:23:43,040
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

324
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:48,880
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

325
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:54,890
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

326
00:23:54,890 --> 00:24:00,640
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

327
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:03,600
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

328
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:06,520
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

329
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:12,700
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

330
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:15,370
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

331
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:19,290
<i>for you to come back home</i>

332
00:24:20,140 --> 00:24:22,470
His pure white cape proves that he's

333
00:24:20,710 --> 00:24:23,540
I'm a mild-mannered person,
but even I'm pissed off.

334
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:23,410
This village used to protect the Hero's Sword.

335
00:24:22,470 --> 00:24:24,170
the strongest warrior in the village.

336
00:24:23,410 --> 00:24:25,080
It's a replica.

337
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:27,810
They're a gift to honor warriors
who have worked hard.

338
00:24:24,150 --> 00:24:25,080
Perv.

339
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:26,860
We're not warriors.

340
00:24:26,860 --> 00:24:28,420
Don't tell the rest of the family.

341
00:24:28,420 --> 00:24:29,990
He was a real hero.
